# Let rocm_ipc be selected when the consumer asks for peer error handling.
#
# rocm_ipc already advertises PUT_ZCOPY and GET_ZCOPY, so it is capable of the
# RMA operations NIXL's UCX backend issues.  What it does NOT advertise is
# UCT_IFACE_FLAG_ERRHANDLE_PEER_FAILURE -- and NIXL creates its endpoints with
# UCP_ERR_HANDLING_MODE_PEER by default (src/plugins/ucx/ucx_utils.cpp).  UCX
# drops every transport that cannot do peer error handling from such an
# endpoint, so rocm_ipc is filtered out before protocol selection even looks at
# it, and intra-node GPU-to-GPU transfers fall back to host shared memory or
# TCP.
#
# Provenance: proposed by @anjoj0 in ai-dynamo/nixl#2039, tested there on
# 8x Radeon PRO W7900 (gfx1100) on top of openucx/ucx#11299, where it made all
# four GPU-pair cases select rocm_ipc/rocm_ipc at ~27.4 GB/s READ and
# ~23.5 GB/s WRITE with NIXL's default peer error mode.  As of writing the flag
# is NOT upstream: openucx/ucx master has UCT_IFACE_FLAG_DEVICE_EP from #11299
# but still no ERRHANDLE_PEER_FAILURE, and v1.19.x (what this tree builds) has
# neither.  Drop this patch once it lands.
#
# CAVEAT: this asserts a capability.  Advertising ERRHANDLE_PEER_FAILURE tells
# UCX that rocm_ipc can detect and report a peer that has died; if it cannot,
# the failure mode is a hang rather than NIXL_ERR_REMOTE_DISCONNECT.  The
# proposer exercised 12 cross-NUMA peer-exit runs without a hang, but
# explicitly excluded stale-registration behaviour from the claim.  Treat this
# as an experiment, not a hardening.
#
# NOTE the reporter's baseline was UCX develop/master, which also carries
# #11299 and other changes.  This tree builds ROCm/ucx v1.19.x, so the flag
# alone may not be sufficient here -- that is exactly what we are testing.
#
diff --git a/src/uct/rocm/ipc/rocm_ipc_iface.c b/src/uct/rocm/ipc/rocm_ipc_iface.c
index 67fe0fb..fe19761 100644
--- a/src/uct/rocm/ipc/rocm_ipc_iface.c
+++ b/src/uct/rocm/ipc/rocm_ipc_iface.c
@@ -124,7 +124,8 @@ static ucs_status_t uct_rocm_ipc_iface_query(uct_iface_h tl_iface,
     iface_attr->cap.flags               = UCT_IFACE_FLAG_GET_ZCOPY |
                                           UCT_IFACE_FLAG_PUT_ZCOPY |
                                           UCT_IFACE_FLAG_PENDING   |
-                                          UCT_IFACE_FLAG_CONNECT_TO_IFACE;
+                                          UCT_IFACE_FLAG_CONNECT_TO_IFACE |
+                                          UCT_IFACE_FLAG_ERRHANDLE_PEER_FAILURE;
 
     iface_attr->latency = ucs_linear_func_make(iface->config.latency, 0);
     iface_attr->bandwidth.dedicated     = 0;
